<div class="mhxrguide-wrap">

    <div class="mhxrguide-hero">
        <span class="mhxrguide-kicker">Private Server</span>
        <h1 class="mhxrguide-title">How to Play</h1>
        <p class="mhxrguide-sub">
            Monster Hunter Explore's official servers were shut down by Capcom in 2020. This is a
            private, non-commercial restoration server so the game can still be played — here is
            everything you need to get connected.
        </p>
    </div>

    @* ---- Step 1: il gioco ---- *@
    <div class="mhxrguide-card">
        <div class="mhxrguide-step-head">
            <span class="mhxrguide-step-num">1</span>
            <h2 class="mhxrguide-step-title">Get the game</h2>
        </div>
        <p>
            You need your own copy of Monster Hunter Explore (.apk). This tool does not contain or
            download the game for you.
        </p>
        <div class="mhxrguide-warn">
            <strong>Japanese version only.</strong> The Taiwan build has an anti-tampering check
            (AppGuard) that blocks any APK re-signed with a different key — which is exactly what
            patching does. With the Taiwan version the game opens and closes immediately, with no
            error, no matter what you try. The
            Japanese version does not have it and works normally.
        </div>
        <p>The link below is the one that worked for me:</p>
        <a class="mhxrguide-btn"
           href="https://apkpure.com/%E3%83%A2%E3%83%B3%E3%82%B9%E3%82%BF%E3%83%BC%E3%83%8F%E3%83%B3%E3%82%BF%E3%83%BC-%E3%82%A8%E3%82%AF%E3%82%B9%E3%83%97%E3%83%AD%E3%82%A2/jp.co.capcom.android.explore/download"
           target="_blank"
           rel="noopener">
            📥 Download the APK (Japanese)
        </a>
    </div>

    @* ---- Step 2: Java ---- *@
    <div class="mhxrguide-card">
        <div class="mhxrguide-step-head">
            <span class="mhxrguide-step-num">2</span>
            <h2 class="mhxrguide-step-title">Install Java (JDK, not JRE)</h2>
        </div>
        <p>
            The patcher uses <code>keytool</code>, which only exists in the JDK. This is the most
            common thing people get wrong: searching "Java download" usually gets you the JRE, and
            the patcher will say Java is missing even though you can see it installed.
        </p>
        <p>Get <strong>Eclipse Temurin JDK 17</strong> (free) and pick "JDK", not "JRE", on the page.</p>
        <a class="mhxrguide-btn mhxrguide-btn-alt" href="https://adoptium.net" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            ☕ Get the JDK
        </a>
    </div>

    @* ---- Step 3: prima di disinstallare ---- *@
    <div class="mhxrguide-card">
        <div class="mhxrguide-step-head">
            <span class="mhxrguide-step-num">3</span>
            <h2 class="mhxrguide-step-title">Before you do anything else — read this</h2>
        </div>
        <p>
            A patched APK has a different signature, and Android will not install it over the game
            you already have — you will need to <strong>uninstall</strong> it first. Uninstalling
            also wipes the app's local storage, which is where the game keeps your "ID card".
            Reinstalling without it means the server does not recognize you and you start over.
        </p>
        <div class="mhxrguide-warn">
            Your character is <strong>not</strong> lost — it lives in the server's database, not on
            your phone. But you need the <strong>transfer code</strong> to reclaim it, and it has to
            be set up <strong>before</strong> you uninstall.
        </div>
        <ol class="mhxrguide-list">
            <li>Open the game you have right now</li>
            <li>Set up account transfer and write down the code and password</li>
            <li>Save them somewhere that is <strong>not</strong> your phone</li>
            <li>Only then uninstall</li>
        </ol>
        <p>
            Skip this and your character stays in the database with no way to reconnect it — I can
            fix that from my side, but you can't do it yourself, so it's much simpler to just save
            the code first.
        </p>
    </div>

    @* ---- Step 4: il patcher ---- *@
    <div class="mhxrguide-card">
        <div class="mhxrguide-step-head">
            <span class="mhxrguide-step-num">4</span>
            <h2 class="mhxrguide-step-title">Download and run MHXR Patcher</h2>
        </div>
        <p>
            My own tool: it takes your APK and changes two things — the server address, so the game
            points here instead of Capcom's dead servers, and optionally the text language.
        </p>
        <a class="mhxrguide-btn" href="https://github.com/Heroic853/MHXR_Patcher_Heroic853" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            📥 Download MHXR Patcher
        </a>
        <p>Full instructions and source are on that page.</p>

        <div class="mhxrguide-note">
            <strong>"Windows protected your PC"</strong> — normal, it happens to any program that
            isn't signed with a paid certificate. Click "More info", then "Run anyway".<br />
            <strong>Antivirus flags it? Add an exclusion to Windows Defender</strong>
            for the folder you put it in if this happens.
        </div>

        <img src="images/MhxrPatcherScreenshot.png" alt="MHXR Patcher application window" class="mhxrguide-screenshot" />

        <ol class="mhxrguide-list">
            <li><strong>Browse</strong> — pick your game's .apk file</li>
            <li><strong>Server address</strong> — the address I gave you, max 47 characters (that's the physical space inside the game, not a choice I made)</li>
            <li><strong>Switch the game to English</strong> — optional, and partial: monster names and common menus/errors are translated, quest text and etc...</li>
            <li><strong>Create and save the APK</strong> — pick where to save it on your PC DO NOT SAVE THE NAME OF APK IN JAPANESE</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    @* ---- Step 5: installazione ---- *@
    <div class="mhxrguide-card">
        <div class="mhxrguide-step-head">
            <span class="mhxrguide-step-num">5</span>
            <h2 class="mhxrguide-step-title">Install and connect</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="mhxrguide-note">
            <strong>Want to play from your PC instead of your phone?</strong> Install BlueStacks
            first — it's an Android emulator, it lets the patched APK run on Windows just like it
            would on a phone. Get it before installing the APK below.
        </div>
        <a class="mhxrguide-btn mhxrguide-btn-alt" href="https://www.bluestacks.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            🖥️ Get BlueStacks
        </a>
        <ol class="mhxrguide-list">
            <li>Copy the patched APK to your phone / android emulator and install it — you'll need to allow installs from unknown sources, since it isn't from the Play Store</li>
            <li>Open the game and use account transfer with the code and password from step 3</li>
        </ol>
        <p>That's it — you should be in.</p>
    </div>

    @* ---- Troubleshooting ---- *@
    <div class="mhxrguide-card">
        <h2 class="mhxrguide-step-title" style="margin-bottom: 14px;">If something goes wrong</h2>

        <div class="mhxrguide-faq-item">
            <p class="mhxrguide-faq-q">"java not found" / "keytool not found"</p>
            <p class="mhxrguide-faq-a">You installed the JRE instead of the JDK — see step 2. If you're sure you have the JDK, restart your PC: the install adds Java system-wide, but programs already open don't notice.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mhxrguide-faq-item">
            <p class="mhxrguide-faq-q">"The address is N characters long but the slot only fits 47"</p>
            <p class="mhxrguide-faq-a">The address is too long — ask me if I have a shorter one.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mhxrguide-faq-item">
            <p class="mhxrguide-faq-q">"no address found"</p>
            <p class="mhxrguide-faq-a">The file you picked isn't the game's APK, or it's a version the patcher doesn't recognize.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mhxrguide-faq-item">
            <p class="mhxrguide-faq-q">The APK won't install</p>
            <p class="mhxrguide-faq-a">Almost always the old game is still installed — uninstall it first (but only after saving your transfer code, see step 3).</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mhxrguide-faq-item">
            <p class="mhxrguide-faq-q">The game opens and closes immediately, no error</p>
            <p class="mhxrguide-faq-a">You used the Taiwan version. Only the Japanese version works — see the warning in step 1.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mhxrguide-faq-item">
            <p class="mhxrguide-faq-q">The game opens but won't connect</p>
            <p class="mhxrguide-faq-a">The server address is wrong, or the server is down — message me to check.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    @* ---- Il progetto ---- *@
    <div class="mhxrguide-card">
        <h2 class="mhxrguide-step-title" style="margin-bottom: 12px;">About this project</h2>
        <p>
            A private, non-commercial restoration server for Monster Hunter Explore, built on top of
            the community's original <em>apypos-server</em> project. Not affiliated with Capcom —
            this exists only because the official servers are gone and the game would otherwise be
            unplayable.
        </p>
        <div class="mhxrguide-links">
            <a class="mhxrguide-btn mhxrguide-btn-alt" href="https://github.com/Heroic853/MHXR-ServerHeroic" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                🖥️ Server source
            </a>
            <a class="mhxrguide-btn mhxrguide-btn-alt" href="https://github.com/Heroic853/MHXR_Patcher_Heroic853" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                🛠️ Patcher source
            </a>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mhxrguide-cta">
        <p style="margin-bottom: 14px;">Something not working, or found a bug in-game?</p>
        <a class="mhxrguide-btn" href="mhxr-feedback">
            🎫 Open a ticket
        </a>
    </div>

</div>
